# Changes in 1.4.0:
#  - ONE armature per win text, built like this: GLOBAL_MASTER > one parent (ROOT) bone per
#    word > one bone per letter. The first word is on top, the next word below it
#    (MASSIVE over WIN). All animations understand words: letters are animated in reading
#    order (top word first), the accordion fans out around the middle of EACH word, and the
#    word parent bones get their own secondary motion.
#  - "Organic" slider (Settings): 0 = the original pure-math motion (sine waves, perfectly
#    even stagger). Higher = irregular multi-frequency motion, uneven start times, every
#    letter a little different (size, tilt, timing), words that lag / overshoot on their own.
#    "Seed" gives a different but repeatable variation.
#
# Changes in 1.3.0 (Blender 5.2 LTS):
#  - Clip layout is the same for all 12 variations:
#        ENTRY  1..30    (last frame 30)
#        LOOP  31..85    (first frame 31 and last frame 85 = the SAME pose)
#        EXIT  86..100   (first frame 86 = the same pose as loop frame 85)
#    Frames 30, 31, 85 and 86 all hold the identical rest pose on every channel.
#  - Rotation axis conversion is now exact: every logical rotation is turned into a
#    rotation matrix, moved into the bone's own space (A^T * R * A) and converted back to
#    XYZ Euler angles - keeping full turns (360 / 540 deg spins) and handling mirrored
#    bones / armatures, multi-axis combinations and gimbal lock.
#  - Build All keeps all 12 actions per rig safe: new actions are built under a temporary
#    name and replace the old one only after they succeeded, a failed build never deletes
#    a good action, fake user is always on, your own active action is protected, the
#    previously active action is restored, and everything is verified afterwards
#    (count, keys, identical poses at 30/31/85/86). "Verify Actions" runs the same check.
#  - Keys are written straight into the F-Curves of a slotted Action (independent of your
#    keying settings); the old keyframe_insert code stays as an automatic fallback.
#  - Rig Creator: bones line up with the world axes, a space between words is kept, safe
#    rollback if a creation fails. Safe to run again from the Text Editor.

